{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And Jacob feared.</b> He feared that the merit of honoring father and mother might avail Esau, for he [Jacob] had not fulfilled it, since twenty years had already passed. Or alternatively, that the merit of the land of Israel might avail him [Esau], while he [Jacob] had been outside the land." "<b>And he was distressed.</b> He was distressed over the fact that he feared Esau, after the Holy One, blessed be He, had promised him. From Rabbi Eliav the Priest, of blessed memory. Another explanation: ויירא — as I explained; ויצר לו — because he heard that he was coming toward him to kill him, and at first he [Esau] had said ״יקרבו ימי אבל אבי ואהרגה״ etc., so he [Jacob] said: if so, Isaac my father is certainly dead. And this explains why it says ״אלהי אבי יצחק,״ even though one does not designate the name of the Holy One, blessed be He, upon a person as long as he is alive."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:31.861440278Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}